  "strings": {
    "\n          {b}Folders read in the browser are matched by name, not verified.{b_}\n          The File System Access API gives the browser a folder's name, never its\n          path — so two reports appear to share a folder when the names match. On\n          one analyst's machine {s}Stock_RDC{s_} may be a network\n          share and on another a local copy. Treat a folder link as a lead to\n          confirm, not a fact. {b}A source read by the desktop app is different:{b_}\n          the app reports the full path of the folder and of every file it read,\n          and a fingerprint of that path (the root id), so you can see which exact\n          file was used. That path is what the app says about its own machine, not\n          something the platform has checked, and sources are still grouped by\n          folder name: two same-named folders at different paths show as one\n          source with the path from the latest run — compare the root id.\n          GreenPlum sources are exact: the connection name is a\n          server-side alias. Dates come from each file's modification time as the\n          analyst's own machine reported it.\n        ": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/data_sources.html:163"
    },
    "(wide format HOU/RM/CM/TMR) or manual file in long format (columns person/role/node/parent). «Verify» will not save anything — only show how many rows were recognised. «Import» fully replaces the previous export (manual grants are not affected).": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/admin_scopes.html:61"
    },
